  "prefLabel": "Jus 419.01 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Jus 419.01 Definitions. For purposes of RSA 292:6-a, the following terms shall have the following meanings:\n\n(a) “Of the same immediate family” means a spouse, parent, grandparent, child, grandchild, sibling, or half-sibling, including a stepparent, step grandparent, stepchild, step grandchild, stepsibling, and step half-sibling.\n\n(b) “Related by blood or marriage” means, in addition to any member of the same immediate family, as that term is defined in Jus 419.01(a), the following:\n\ni. An uncle, aunt, nephew, niece, or first cousin;\n\nii. A step uncle, step aunt, step nephew, step niece, or first step cousin; and\n\niii. A parent-in-law, child-in-law, sibling-in-law, half-sibling-in-law, grandparent-in-law, grandchild-in-law, uncle-in-law, aunt-in-law, nephew-in-law, niece-in-law, or first cousin-in-law.\n\nSource. #14162, eff 12-27-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/jus400.html"
